 of Japan's largest and most populous island of Honshu. As of 2020, the city had a population of 1.46 million, making it the ninth-most populous city in Japan. More than half (56.8%) of Kyoto Prefecture's population resides in the city. The city is the cultural anchor of the substantially larger Greater Kyoto, a metropolitan statistical area home to approximately 3.8 million people. It is also part of the even larger Keihanshin metropolitan area, along with Osaka and Kobe.","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Kyoto%2C_Japan_%2849667780482%29.jpg/330px-Kyoto%2C_Japan_%2849667780482%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kyoto"},"twins":["Q365","Q2044","Q1899","Q5826","Q9022","Q1435","Q1085","Q90","Q100","Q5582862","Q23436","Q27494","Q42144","Q31487"],"climate":{"temp":[3.6,4.5,7.6,12.8,17.9,22.1,26.2,27,23.3,17.3,11.5,6],"rain":[97,92,114,119,140,178,210,149,192,161,96,109],"cloud":[83,80,73,69,70,80,77,66,73,68,70,78]}}